Extension API: move pops with one command instead of a click chain.

Adds `MSG_SET_JOBS` (0x84) — one colony, a list of (pop_idx,
new_job), applied whole or not at all. Fundament entry 52 is the
decision; `doc/briefs/90-pop-move-one-command-instead-of-a-click-chain.md`
is the brief; Run A (`d98a96d` in the OrionLayer tree) is the source
reading it rests on.

STATUS: needed to retire the RESORT / ESTABLISH / PICK / DROP click
chain, which costs four snapshot round trips per drop and has to
steer the game's own ten-row window first. NOT YET APPLIED.

    TO APPLY, to the orion2re working tree at ~/orion2re
    (engine 1.60.0, git cf4d9617):

        cd ~/orion2re && patch -p1 < \
            ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_move_pop.patch

    and it comes back off with

        cd ~/orion2re && patch -R -p1 < \
            ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_move_pop.patch

    FIVE FILES, AND ONLY TWO OF THEM ARE JOES'. `src/ext/` is our
    own directory and is untracked in his tree, so the three files
    there diverge from nothing. What touches his code is
    `src/game/colmove.h` and `src/game/colmove.cpp`, five hunks
    between them, and every line either sits inside
    `#ifdef ORION2RE_EXT` or is a rename of a call site to a
    wrapper that is unconditional. A build without the flag is his
    code doing exactly what it did: verified by compiling the
    patched `colmove.cpp` with and without `-DORION2RE_EXT`.

    THE HUNKS BELOW ARE GENERATED, never hand-edited. They were
    produced by diffing a scratch copy against the pristine files
    (`git show cf4d9617:` for the two of Joes'; the on-disk state
    for the three of ours), then applied forward to a fresh export
    and compared byte for byte. The result also reverse-applies
    cleanly.

WHAT THE COMMAND DOES, AND WHY IT IS SHAPED THIS WAY

    ONE COLONY, A LIST OF POPS. The recalculation in the original
    is per batch, not per pop: `Send_Cluster_` runs its whole
    cluster loop and only then calls `COLONY::Col_Calc_Wrapper_`
    (colmove.cpp:461-464, and the early-exit path at :145-148). A
    list therefore reproduces the engine's own grouping; N single
    commands would run `Colony_Calculation_` N times and produce a
    sequence of intermediate states the original never produces.

    THE RULES ARE NOT RE-IMPLEMENTED. `Give_Colonist_New_Job_` is
    called unchanged, once per entry. A second copy of its four
    refusal conditions inside `src/ext/` is exactly the duplicate
    this project keeps paying for, and it would go stale the first
    time Joes touches the function.

    WHAT THE PATCH DOES REMOVE IS THE MESSAGE BOX, NEVER A CHECK.
    All four refusals answer with `GENDRAW::Help_`
    (colmove.cpp:527, :534, :541, :556), which is
    `TEXTBOX::Do_Text_Box_` -> `Text_Box_Get_Input_(0)`, whose
    zero-ticks path is `do { … } while (fields::Get_Input_() == 0)`
    (textbox.cpp:145-149) — a spin waiting for a human. Reached
    from the Extension API's own drain loop that would stop the
    engine, and worse: the inner `Get_Input_()` calls `ext::Tick`
    (fields.cpp:167), so the refusal would recurse into the command
    queue it was called from. `_ext_suppress_refusal_help` turns the
    drawing off for the duration of one command. The refusal still
    happens, still returns 0, and is still the engine's own.

    ALL-OR-NOTHING, AND THIS IS A MARKED DEVIATION. The original
    moves pops until the first refusal and leaves the earlier ones
    moved (colmove.cpp:168-173), because a human is standing at the
    box and can decide whether to continue. A command has nobody to
    ask, so it does not start: the colony's pop words are saved
    before the list is applied and restored whole if any entry is
    refused. The game therefore behaves differently under the
    command than under the click, deliberately. Fundament 52.

    THE PICK-UP IS TRANSCRIBED, not skipped. `Get_Cluster_` clears
    the assigned bit on every pop it takes, and `Send_Cluster_`
    re-flags them one at a time, so `Sum_Colonists_` never counts a
    pop that is in the air. The handler clears the bit on the whole
    list first for the same reason — without it, a list that moves
    one pop out of Food and another in would check the second
    against a Food count that still included the first.

    A POP ALREADY IN THE JOB IT WAS ASKED FOR is re-flagged and NOT
    rule-checked, which is colmove.cpp:165-166 and is why an
    android returning to its own column lands where rule 2 would
    refuse it. Transcribed, not tidied.

    THREE GUARDS ARE OURS AND ARE NOT TRANSCRIPTIONS: the colony
    must be the local player's, the indices must be in range, and
    the game must not be holding a cluster. The original reaches
    this code from a screen that cannot show another player's
    colony and cannot have a cluster in hand at the same time; an
    API can be sent anything.

WHAT IS NOT IN THIS PATCH

    No serialization change. Nothing new is reported back: the
    client learns the result from the state snapshot it already
    reads, by diffing the pop words it predicted. No field-list
    change, no framebuffer change, no `PROTO_VERSION` bump — the
    protocol did not change shape, one message id was added, and
    `tools/version_check.py` is what fails on an engine that does
    not have it.

